# Plico (太初) — Project Rules for Cline

## Project
Rust (edition 2021). AI-native OS kernel. Inference-framework-agnostic.

## Build & Test
```bash
cargo build
EMBEDDING_BACKEND=stub LLM_BACKEND=stub cargo test --lib    # fast unit tests
cargo clippy -- -D warnings                                  # zero warnings
```

## Coding Standards
- `snake_case.rs` files, one concept per file, < 300 lines
- `snake_case` functions, `PascalCase` types
- No `#[allow(clippy::...)]` — fix the issue
- No `unsafe` without `# Safety` comment
- `thiserror` typed errors, no panics in lib code
- `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` inline in source files

## Architecture Constraints
- Dependency: `api/bin → kernel → tool/fs/intent → cas/memory/scheduler/temporal/llm`
- `kernel/` is the only module importing all others
- CAS is the only module touching the host filesystem
- All persistence uses `atomic_write_json()` — never `std::fs::write()`

## Testing
- Always use stub backends: `EMBEDDING_BACKEND=stub LLM_BACKEND=stub`
- Kernel test helper: `crate::kernel::tests::make_kernel()` → `(Arc<AIKernel>, TempDir)`
- Stub embedding returns empty vectors — don't assert search result counts

## Security
- Reserved agent names: `kernel`, `system`, `root`, `admin`
- Max content: 10 MB per object
- No hardcoded API keys
